      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the usual maximum single oral dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This could cause hepatotoxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day), a common standard regimen.\n2. **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day), the usual ceiling.\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another regimen you prefer.\n4. **2000 mg three times daily as written**, if it's intentional. I'd need you to confirm that explicitly, and I'd add a note on the order documenting the rationale.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
